    "raw_text": "Kauffman Announces $1.61 Million in Funding for Local Projects\nSeptember 15, 2026\nHARRISBURG – State Rep. Rob Kauffman (R-Franklin) has helped secure more than $1.61 million in Local Share Account (LSA) grant funding for local infrastructure projects and equipment purchases for area organizations that benefit the community.\n“I’m pleased to announce these grants, which will ensure these beneficial projects move forward,” said Kauffman. “I will always advocate for funding for our community centers, fire companies and emergency management projects. I admire and love working with organizations such as Habitat for Humanity, as they bring the community together to meet housing needs. The upgrades to the Corker Hill Mansion in Scotland (a site on the National Register of Historic Places) will allow more people to experience and enjoy the history of Scotland and this beautiful mansion.”\nThe following were awarded grants:\n•\nChambersburg Borough - $400,000\nfor infrastructure improvements to the Eugene C. Clark, Jr. Community Center, including a new HVAC system, air conditioning throughout the facility, new windows in the gymnasium and bathroom upgrades.\n•\nFranklin County Area Development Corporation - $97,931\nto purchase a box truck for Habitat for Humanity of Franklin County.\n•\nFranklin County Area Development Corporation - $358,130\nfor the purchase and installation of an emergency generator at Menno-Haven’s Life Center. This system will better ensure the safety of nearly 2,000 residents and staff in cases of emergency.\n•\nGreene Township - $136,666\nfor the purchase and installation of an HVAC system at the historic Corker Hill Mansion.\n•\nGuilford Township - $92,000\nto complete an HVAC replacement project at South Mountain Volunteer Fire Department.\n“I also worked with Sen. Doug Mastriano (R-Franklin) to secure an additional $524,491 in grants for a new pumper tank for the Fayetteville Volunteer Fire Department and renovations at Totem Pole Playhouse.”\nGrant award details are as follows:\n•\nGuilford Township, on behalf of Fayetteville Volunteer Fire Department - $312,191\nfor a new Seagrave Marauder Fire Engine to replace a 30-year-old fire truck that has reached the end of its useful life.\n•\nGreene Township, on behalf of Totem Pole Playhouse - $212,300\nto replace the deteriorating cedar siding and aging roof on the main theater and adjacent office building.\nThe grants were approved and awarded by the Commonwealth Financing Authority, which was established as an independent agency that holds fiduciary responsibility over the funding of programs and investments in Pennsylvania’s economic growth. LSA grants are derived from gaming revenues.\nRepresentative Rob Kauffman\n89th District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tricia Lehman\n717.772.9840\ntlehman@pahousegop.com\nRepKauffman.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
